# SMTP credentials for the contact form email sending (POST /api/contact).
# The route uses Nodemailer with Gmail SMTP. SMTP_USER is the Gmail address
# that sends the emails. SMTP_PASS must be an app password for that same
# account. Gmail never accepts the regular account password here. If the
# login is rejected with error 534 and "Application-specific password
# required", the value in SMTP_PASS is not a valid app password.
#
# How to create an app password:
# 1. Sign in to the Google account that matches SMTP_USER.
# 2. Turn on 2 Step Verification in the Google Account security settings.
# 3. In the same settings, open App passwords and generate one for Mail.
# 4. Copy the 16 character code into SMTP_PASS. Spaces are optional.
#
# Never put a real password in this example file. Copy it to .env.local,
# which is gitignored, and fill in your own values for local testing.
# Emails are only sent when both values are set.
SMTP_USER=your_gmail_address@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your_16_character_gmail_app_password
